{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And he said to the people.</b> On that very day. <b>Be ready.</b> For the need of the third day — and this day, which would be the giving of the Torah, and in what matter: <b>Do not approach a woman.</b> From now until after the giving of the Torah." "<b>For three days.</b> According to its plain sense, for the third day, and Moses did not add even one day on his own authority. A parallel: ״ויאסף אותם אל משמר שלשת ימים״, and there it says ״ויאמר אליהם יוסף ביום השלישי״, and it says ״בעוד שלשת ימים״, and it is written there ״ביום השלישי יום הולדת את פרעה״. After the fifth day of the month and the sixth day of the week had passed, he did what is written in the portion משפטים: ״וישכם בבקר״ etc., until ״שבטי ישראל״."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:58:49.728368177Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}